    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **46 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe spec \u2014 reject a supplied `registrationDate` later than the server date with a 400 \u2014 is covered by `Cp33Tests`. I implemented it following the existing OfficeFloor patterns in this repo (mirroring how the optional `postcode` validation works):\n\n1. **`OwnerRegistrationDate`** (validation helper) \u2014 `validate(request)` rejects a supplied `registrationDate` that is `isAfter(LocalDate.now())`. An absent date, or one on or before today, passes. The check is on the raw supplied date, before any business-day adjustment, so the existing weekend-roll behaviour (Cp07) is untouched.\n\n2. **`FutureRegistrationDateException`** \u2014 a checked exception (so it appears in the `throws` clause), plus **`FutureRegistrationDateExceptionHandler`** responding `400 Bad Request` with body `{\"errors\":[\"registrationDate\"]}`, consistent with the postcode handler.\n\n3. **Escalation YAML** \u2014 `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.FutureRegistrationDateException.yml` wiring the exception to its handler.\n\n4. **`ValidateOwnerFields`** (first step of `POST /api/owners`) \u2014 now calls `OwnerRegistrationDate.validate(request)` and declares the new checked exception. Being the first pipeline step, an invalid date is rejected as a 400 before the transaction/persistence steps run.\n\nI scoped the change to owner creation (POST), matching the spec and test. The update path (`PUT`, via `ApplyOwner`) ignores `registrationDate` entirely \u2014 it's never applied on update \u2014 so no future-date can be stored there.",
